The generator builds on the theLook eCommerce dataset published by Looker
on the Google Cloud Marketplace (bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce).
The files in src/data/ come from the upstream repository unchanged.

Changes made in this repository (Apache 2.0, section 4(b)):

- images/ (a demo GIF) was not copied.
- src/data/world_pop.csv is stored with LF line endings instead of CRLF
  (the repository's .gitattributes normalises all text files). The
  generator reads it in text mode, which accepts both.
- Dockerfile: base image pinned by version and digest; dependencies
  installed from requirements.lock (all versions pinned, with hashes)
  instead of the unpinned requirements.txt; runs as a non-root user;
  ENTRYPOINT fixed to generator.py (upstream ran data_generator.py, which
  does not exist).
- requirements.lock: added (generated with uv pip compile from
  requirements.txt, which is unchanged).
- generator.py: --db-password defaults to the DB_PASSWORD environment
  variable, and the startup log line no longer prints the password.
- Clickstream events are written to MongoDB (database web, collection
  events, one document per event, _id = event id) instead of the
  PostgreSQL events table: new src/mongo_writer.py, new --mongo-* flags
  (password from the MONGO_PASSWORD environment variable), pymongo added
  to requirements.txt and requirements.lock; MongoDB errors count as
  database errors in the main loop. The PostgreSQL events table is still
  created but no longer written.
- Synthetic additions, labelled in the code (cahier des charges 4.3):
  cart events carry product_id and price (src/models.py); basket affinity,
  where each item after the first is, with probability
  --basket-affinity-prob (default 0.6), one of the first item's fixed
  companion products (--companions, default 5; 0 = any product of its
  category); a popularity skew on each order's first item
  (--popularity-skew, Zipf exponent, default 0.8). Setting the probability
  and the skew to 0 restores the upstream behaviour.
- Every change is visible in the Git history of this directory.
